## Findings
1. advisory — packages/commands/src/ui-capture-comments.ts:203 `appendUiCaptureComment` reads `input.viewport.width` before `commentProblem` runs. An authenticated POST whose `viewport` is missing or `null` therefore throws, and the server answers 500 `{ error: "internal error" }` instead of the brief:43 refusal `{ ok:false, exitCode:1, output }`. Nothing is appended, so the write still fails closed. brief:72 makes "absent or wrong type" a limit, so this is not blocking. The same uncaught-throw-to-500 path has three more sites: apps/server/src/http.ts:800, where `decodeURIComponent` throws on a malformed `%` (for example `/api/ui-capture-image/W-1/%E0`), which brief:72 also lists as a limit; and packages/cli/src/serve.ts:105, where `captureSourceTree`'s `git rev-parse` throws outside a repository, on all three injected routes. Fix: run `commentProblem` on the input before comparing bindings, and catch decode errors as 404. [severity: S3] [class: spec×input-without-named-rejector] — check: none: a W-488-b3 served POST without `viewport` expecting HTTP 200 `{ok:false,exitCode:1}` and no new timeline line, plus a GET of `/api/ui-capture-image/W-1/%E0` expecting 404
2. advisory — packages/commands/src/ui-capture-comments.ts:217 The record copies the caller's `viewport` and `pin` objects whole, so extra nested keys pass `commentProblem` and are stored. With a valid token, a pin such as `{x,y,pad:"…1.5 MB"}` gets past the field limits brief:51 promises ("one bounded record"). It also pushes `timeline/patron.jsonl` over the 1 MiB read cap, which then shuts every later comment append and every UI build-review packet for this studio, not just the bad record. This needs a token and extra keys are an unlisted form under brief:70, so it is an advisory. Fix: rebuild `{ x, y }` and `{ width, height }` from the validated values. Readers reached: `readUiCaptureComments` (line 161) and `scripts/review-packet.mjs:426`. [severity: S3] [class: review×unredacted-writes-to-tracked-files] — check: none: a W-488-b2 case appending a pin with an extra key and asserting the stored `record.pin` deepEquals `{x,y}`
3. advisory — studio/ci/shots/W-488/*.png and manifest.txt are on the branch, although brief:35 excludes "committed PNGs and `studio/ci/shots/`". They are the served-e2e gate's own output for a kind-ui opus (the certificate is in studio/ci/W-488-served-e2e-7dee6c69.log), not files written by hand. The source diff outside studio/ is exactly the seven Files owned. The brief's wording should say that gate-produced shots are allowed. [severity: S4] [class: spec×stale-citation-residue] — check: none: a brief-admission rule that separates gate-written `ci/shots/<opus>/` from owned paths
4. advisory — docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:225 describes the `#/captures[/<opus>]` console route as if it reads the capture sets now, but brief:23 moves that route to the web half and this opus does not mount it. The read-path mermaid `posts` node also leaves out `/ui-capture-comment`. [severity: S4] [class: docs×architecture-graph-not-regenerated] — check: none: a docs check that every route in http.ts's ROUTE_INDEX_HTML appears in the ARCHITECTURE read-path graph

